{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Ibn Majah","section":{"33":{"eng-name":"Etiquette","ara-name":"كتاب الأدب"}},"section_detail":{"33":{"hadithnumber_first":3657,"hadithnumber_last":3826,"arabicnumber_first":3657,"arabicnumber_last":3826}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":3708,"arabicnumber":3708,"text":"Rapporté par Ali : J’avais deux moments pour rendre visite au Messager d’Allah ﷺ, la nuit et le jour. Si j’arrivais alors qu’il priait, il s’éclaircissait la gorge pour me faire comprendre qu’il était en prière","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}],"reference":{"book":33,"hadith":52},"chapter":{"id":17,"ara-name":"باب الاِسْتِئْذَانِ","eng-name":"Seeking Permission to Enter","isFirstHadith":false}}]}